# Benchmark outputs
#
# Benchmark results stay in Git: the README's performance claim, the site's
# benchmark ledger, and `scripts/verify-site-bench-data.mjs` all read the
# checked-in report, so a run that is not committed cannot be verified. The
# rule below therefore only hides incidental local files and keeps the two
# artifacts the harnesses publish — the dated snapshot and the `latest`
# pointer that copies it.
benchmarks/*/results/*
!benchmarks/*/results/.gitkeep
!benchmarks/*/results/latest.json
!benchmarks/*/results/latest.md
!benchmarks/*/results/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.json
!benchmarks/*/results/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.md
benchmarks/*/.swc/

# Browser verification artifacts
.vitest-attachments/
coverage/

# Effective Flow runtime state
.effective-flow/
docs/plan/

# Local extraction cache (ADR-019)
.palamedes/
